# Kimpor Kang — Construction Portfolio Website

## 1. Project Purpose

Personal single-page portfolio for **Kimpor Kang**, a junior Civil Engineering
student at Paragon International University (Phnom Penh) who works as Project
Coordinator at **Singbuild Construction Co., Ltd.** (design & build contractor,
est. 2015). The site presents real construction / interior fit-out project
experience, skills, side projects, and contact info. Target audience: employers,
clients, and engineering contacts in Phnom Penh and beyond.

## 2. Tech Stack & Constraints

- **Plain HTML5 + CSS3 + vanilla JavaScript** — no frameworks, no bundlers,
  no npm dependencies, no build step.
- Fonts loaded from Google Fonts CDN: `Yantramanav` (headings, menu, labels,
  counters) and `Poppins` (body copy). Site degrades gracefully to system
  fonts offline.
- Deployable as-is on any static host. On Vercel it needs **zero config**
  (no framework, output = repo root, `index.html` entry).
- Do NOT introduce a framework, package.json, or build pipeline unless the
  user explicitly asks — the deliberate simplicity is a design decision.

## 3. File Structure

```
Kimpor-Portfolio-Website/
├── index.html              # The ENTIRE site (single page, ~420 lines)
├── css/
│   └── style.css           # All styling: tokens, layout, responsive (~20 KB)
├── js/
│   └── script.js           # All interactivity (IIFE, strict mode, ES5-safe)
├── images/
│   ├── projects/           # 8 project photo galleries (one folder per project)
│   ├── hero.jpg            # Hero background (Fengfu render)
│   ├── KimporKANG_Portrait.png # Owner's headshot (white studio background)
│   └── portrait-cutout.png # Generated: transparent-background portrait
├── tools/
│   ├── cutout.py           # Removes the white background from the headshot
│   └── build_galleries.py  # Copies + resizes archive photos into the galleries
├── README.md               # Human docs: run, photo map, edit guides
└── kimpor-portfolio.skill  # This file
```

## 4. Design System (css/style.css `:root`)

| Token | Value | Use |
|---|---|---|
| `--navy` | `#00283b` | TPMG brand navy: burger, side menu, stats band, hero strip, footer, badges (`rgba(0,40,59,.86)`) |
| `--navy-2` | `#0a4159` | hovers on navy, text links |
| `--navy-deep` | `#001d2b` | headings, hero veil + fallback background |
| `--paper` | `#ffffff` | page background |
| `--soft` | `#f4f6f8` | alt sections + portrait frame background |
| `--line` | `#e8e8e9` | hairline borders and dividers (TPMG's sticky-header line) |
| `--text` / `--dim` | `#383a40` / `#565969` | body / secondary text |
| `--menu` | `#9aa2ab` | inactive nav menu cells |
| `--ok` / `--live` | `#2f855a` / `#c07a17` | status colours (dots render `#5fd39a` done, `#f0b34e` ongoing, `#7dc4ff` ahead) |
| `--bar` | `72px` | top-bar height (60px under 640px) |
| `--w` | `min(1300px, 92%)` | content width (TPMG uses a 1300px grid) |

- Headings, menu, counters, labels: **Yantramanav** (300/400/500/700) — the
  font TPMG uses. Body copy: **Poppins** (300–600). Both from Google Fonts
  with system fallbacks.
- Signature treatments matched to tpmoralgroup.com: solid-color typography
  only (no ghost/stroke text — the hero title and stat numbers are plain solid
  text); the logo SVG mark is removed and "KIMPOR KANG" is centered in the top
  bar; a navy side menu sliding in from the right; uppercase micro-labels with
  0.1–0.32em letter-spacing; hairline rules; square corners (no border radius
  anywhere).
- Re-theming: colours live only in `:root`; README documents the palette.

## 5. Page Sections (index.html, in order)

1. **Top bar** — white bar; the SVG logo mark is removed and "KIMPOR KANG ·
   Civil Engineering · Phnom Penh" is centered, with equal-width menu cells
   divided by hairlines (`.menu-item[data-nav]`) and a navy hamburger
   (`#navToggle`) at the far right. Menu cells hide below 980px.
2. **Side menu** (`#navPanel`, TPMG style) — the hamburger slides a navy panel
   in from the right (over `.menu-backdrop`, body gets `.menu-open` to lock
   scroll) with numbered `.side-link`s and contact meta; closes via the X
   button (`#navClose`), backdrop click, Escape, or choosing a link.
3. **Hero** — full-bleed `images/hero.jpg` (Fengfu dusk render) under a navy
   veil; eyebrow "Kimpor Kang · Phnom Penh, Cambodia"; the plain **"Civil
   Engineering Portfolio"** title (solid text, no ghost/stroke); sub-line;
   two buttons (`.btn-solid`, `.btn-line`); navy bottom strip with the domain.
4. **Stats band** (navy) — four solid-number cells (`.stat-num`), each
   followed by `.stat-kicker` + `.stat-title`: 8 Projects Supported / 5 Delivery
   Completed & handed over / 3 Currently ongoing / 4 Sectors Hotel ·
   Residential · F&B · Office.
5. **About** (`#about`, label `01`) — portrait frame (`#portraitImg` on a
   blueprint-grid background with a navy name plate) beside the bio and a
   hairline `.facts-list` (degree, experience, focus, languages, location).
6. **Projects** (`#projects`, label `02`, soft-grey) — filter buttons
   (All 8 / Completed-Handover 5 / Ongoing 3) + 8 `.card` tiles carrying
   `data-status`; each card has a 16:10 media area that builds a horizontal
   scroll-snap photo gallery (`data-gallery` + `data-total` → `images/
   projects/<slug>/01.jpg` …) with prev/next buttons, a counter, and a
   click-to-open lightbox. Each card also shows a `.badge` with `.dot`,
   title, type line and description.
7. **Skills** (`#skills`, label `03`) — groups A/B (`.skill-group`) with
   `.chip-list` hairline rows.
8. **Side Projects** (`#side-projects`, label `04`, navy section) — two
   translucent `.side-card`s: SB Grab Code Tracker, Manpower Reporting
   Automation.
9. **Contact** (`#contact`, label `05`) — navy-topped `.contact-card` with
   label/value rows. **Contains placeholders**: `[Add your email]`,
   `[Add your phone]`, `[Add your LinkedIn URL]` — update both the visible
   text and the `mailto:` / `tel:` / href attributes.
10. **Footer** — navy bar with JS-injected year and back-to-top link.

Scroll-reveal: elements carry `.reveal`; JS adds `.is-visible` via
IntersectionObserver. Sections use `scroll-margin-top` to clear the sticky bar.

## 6. JavaScript Behavior (js/script.js)

Single IIFE, `'use strict'`, ES5-compatible (var, function expressions) with
modern APIs guarded:
1. Side menu: `#navToggle` ↔ `#navPanel` (`.is-open` slides it in from the
   right), keeps aria-expanded/aria-hidden/label in sync, toggles
   `body.menu-open` (locks scroll + fades `.menu-backdrop`); also closes via
   `#navClose`, backdrop click, Escape, or choosing a link.
2. Scroll reveal via IntersectionObserver; fallback shows everything.
3. Active nav highlighting: second IntersectionObserver over `section[id]`
   toggles `.is-active` on every `[data-nav]` link with a matching hash
   (covers both menu cells and panel links).
4. Project status filter: `.filter-btn[data-filter]` toggles `.is-hidden` on
   `#projectsGrid .card` by matching `data-status`; re-adds `.is-visible` so
   filtered cards don't re-animate.
5. Project photo galleries: each `.card-media[data-gallery]` builds a
   scroll-snap strip from `images/projects/<slug>/01.jpg`…`data-total`, with
   prev/next buttons, a live counter, and click-to-open lightbox navigation
   (Esc / ← / → supported).
6. Footer year via `new Date().getFullYear()`.

Keep new JS in the same IIFE style; no external libraries.
## 7. Content Inventory — 8 Project Galleries

Photos live in `images/projects/<slug>/` as `01.jpg`, `02.jpg`, … A card's
`data-total` attribute in `index.html` controls how many photos load; the first
file (`01.jpg`) is the card cover. Rebuild all galleries from the source archive
at `D:\SingBuild's Document` with:

```
python tools/build_galleries.py
```

(The archive's Norodom folder holds ~38,000 photos / 6.5 GB, so an even sample
from its latest month is used; Fengfu has no photo folder — its 16 3D renders
are used instead.)

| # | Card | Slug | Status |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | Norodom Business Center | `norodom-business-center/` | Ongoing |
| 2 | UVP2 - Retilling Work | `uvp2-retiling/` | Completed |
| 3 | UVP2 - Common Areas | `uvp2-common-areas/` | Completed |
| 4 | UVP2 - Swimming Pool | `uvp2-swimming-pool/` | Completed |
| 5 | Singapore Airlines Office | `singapore-airlines/` | Completed |
| 6 | Fengfu | `fengfu/` | Ongoing |
| 7 | KFK - KMALL 2 | `kfk-kmall2/` | Completed |
| 8 | UVP2 - Penthouse P5 | `uvp2-penthouse-p5/` | Ongoing |

Hero stats (8 / 5 / 3 / 4 in the stats band and filter counts) must stay in
sync with card count and statuses. The hero background is `images/hero.jpg`.
Full photo-source mapping table lives in README.md.

## 8. Content Boundaries (Privacy)

- Deliberately excluded projects: `15. Akram (Show House)`,
  `16. KFK - Domrey Park` (per owner instruction).
- Never surface HR/personal data (payroll, reviews, Work & HR Records).
- Photos should avoid recognizable worker faces and client-sensitive pricing.
- Contact details are placeholders until the owner supplies real ones.

## 9. Running & Deploying

- **Local:** double-click `index.html`, or `python -m http.server 8000`.
- **GitHub:** repo `KangKimpor/Kimpor-Portfolio-Website`, default branch `main`.
- **Live site:** https://kimpor-portfolio-website.vercel.app
- **Vercel project:** `kimpor-portfolio-website` (scope `kimporkang01-3264s-projects`),
  linked to the GitHub repo via `vercel git connect`, so **every push to `main`
  auto-deploys production** and branches/PRs get preview URLs.
- **Static, zero-config:** no build command, no output directory override,
  framework preset "Other" (files served from repo root).
- **Manual deploy (if needed):**
  ```
  vercel link --yes --project kimpor-portfolio-website --scope kimporkang01-3264s-projects
  vercel --prod
  ```
  Check state with `vercel ls` and open the dashboard at
  https://vercel.com/kimporkang01-3264s-projects/kimpor-portfolio-website
- **Vercel Authentication (SSO) protection is OFF** — the site must stay
  publicly viewable (it is a portfolio).

### Repo conventions

- `.gitignore` excludes `.vercel`, `.env.local`, OS/editor junk.
- Commit history starts at "Initial commit: Kimpor Kang construction portfolio
  site"; the README carries the human-facing docs and photo-source map.


## 10. Maintenance Cookbook

- **Update contact info:** edit `#contact` in index.html; update text AND
  `mailto:` / `tel:` / LinkedIn href.
- **Add a project card:** copy an existing `<article class="card">` block, set
  `data-status`, add image to `images/projects/`, and bump the filter counts,
  stats band and README table.
- **Regenerate the portrait cutout:**
  `python tools/cutout.py images/KimporKANG_Portrait.png images/portrait-cutout.png images/_portrait-preview.png`
  — writes `images/portrait-cutout.png` plus a navy-backed
  `_portrait-preview.png`. Requires Pillow + numpy. Missing cutout falls
  back to `KimporKANG_Portrait.png`, then to the faded "KK" tile.
- **Swap the hero image:** change the `src` of `.hero-img` — pick a landscape
  shot with a clear band for the centred headline (test under the navy veil).
- **Re-theme:** all colours live in `:root` (`--navy*`, `--soft`, `--line`,
  `--text`, `--dim`, `--menu`). Keep it restrained; status dots are the only
  other colours.
- **Commit style:** small, imperative commits; static assets welcome in git
  (total images ≈ 3.5 MB, well under limits).

